::recipe
conversion stage: initial

name: Chocolate Chip Cookies
source: https://publicdomainrecipes.com/chocolate-chip-cookies/
source author: mfed3
source license: Public domain (Unlicense)
ingredients: US
units: mixed
category: baking
tags: cookies, chocolate
yield: as many cookies as the chosen scoop size produces
active time: ~10m
total time: ~20m
image: chocolate-chip-cookies.webp

::ingredients

(butter, melted) 230g / 2 sticks
(flour; bread) 330g
(salt) 5g
(baking soda) 5g
(sugar; white) 100-200g
(sugar; brown) 100-200g
(egg) 1
(milk) 15g
(vanilla) 5g

(chocolate chips) =
    (chocolate chips, dark, 50-70%) 225g
    -OR-
    (chocolate chips, semi-sweet milk) 225g

::equipment

(oven)
(bowl) 2
(mixer or whisk)
(ice cream scoop or spoon)
(baking sheet)
(parchment paper)
(cooling rack)

::instructions

(oven) <heat, 375f>

{dry} =
    (flour) +
    (baking soda) +
    (salt)

{wet} =
    (butter) +
    (sugar; white) +
    (sugar; brown) +
    (egg) +
    (vanilla) +
    (milk)

{wet} <beat, mixer or whisk, a few minutes>

{dough} =
    {wet} +
    {dry} +
    (chocolate chips)

{dough} <stir>

Repeat [
    {dough} <scoop, uniform balls, preferred size>
        <space, evenly, parchment-lined baking sheet>
]
until {dough} used

Repeat [
    {cookies} <bake, one baking sheet at a time, 8-10m, until starting to brown>
]
until baking sheets cooked

{cookies} <cool, a few minutes>
    <transfer, cooling rack>
